      "body": "## Summary\n\n`OffsetProgressiveCurve.initialize()` validates `slope18` but performs no validation on `offset18`, silently accepting\nzero. When `offset18 = 0`, the stored `OFFSET = wrap(0)` contributes nothing to any formula, making the contract\nmathematically identical to `ProgressiveCurve`. This means the contract inherits the `previewWithdraw` arithmetic\nunderflow revert already confirmed in `ProgressiveCurve`: after the first deposit, `previewWithdraw` panics for any\nfull-pool withdrawal query because `divUp(assets, HALF_SLOPE)` exceeds `square(totalShares)` due to the floor-sqrt\nrounding in the deposit path. The contract is non-upgradeable, so a deployer who passes `offset18 = 0` cannot recover\nwithout redeployment and repointing every vault that references the broken curve address. EIP-4626 Section 4 explicitly\nrequires preview functions MUST NOT revert for valid inputs.\n\n## Vulnerability details\n\n### Finding description and impact\n\n**Root cause — asymmetric parameter validation in `initialize()`:**\n\n```solidity\n// OffsetProgressiveCurve.sol L62–L66\nif (slope18 == 0 || slope18 % 2 != 0) revert OffsetProgressiveCurve_InvalidSlope();\n\nSLOPE     = wrap(slope18);\nHALF_SLOPE = wrap(slope18 / 2);\nOFFSET    = wrap(offset18);   // <-- NO VALIDATION: offset18=0 silently accepted\n```\n\n`slope18` is validated; `offset18` is not. Passing `offset18 = 0` stores `OFFSET = wrap(0)` and deploys successfully.\n\n**How OFFSET = 0 collapses the contract to ProgressiveCurve:**\n\nThe distinguishing feature of `OffsetProgressiveCurve` is the additive offset applied to the share count before curve\ncalculations. With `OFFSET = wrap(0)`, every occurrence of `add(wrap(totalShares), OFFSET)` reduces to\n`wrap(totalShares)` — the formula becomes identical to `ProgressiveCurve`. Specifically in `previewWithdraw`:\n\n```solidity\n// OffsetProgressiveCurve.sol — previewWithdraw(), L144–L157\nUD60x18 s = add(wrap(totalShares), OFFSET);\n// When OFFSET = wrap(0):\n// s = add(wrap(totalShares), wrap(0)) = wrap(totalShares)   ← identical to ProgressiveCurve\n```\n\n**Inherited underflow — concrete proof (slope = 2e18, HALF_SLOPE = 1e18, offset = 0):**\n\n| Step                         | Computation                                                  | Result                |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------- |\n| Deposit 2 wei (empty pool)   | `floor(sqrt(2 × 1e18))`                                      | `shares = 1414213562` |\n| `square(wrap(1414213562))`   | `floor(1414213562² / 1e18)` = `floor(1.9999… × 10¹⁸ / 10¹⁸)` | = **1** (raw UD60x18) |\n| `divUp(wrap(2), HALF_SLOPE)` | `ceil(2 × 1e18 / 1e18)`                                      | = **2** (raw UD60x18) |\n| `sub(wrap(1), wrap(2))`      | underflow                                                    | **REVERT**            |\n\nThe revert occurs because the floor-sqrt rounding in `_convertToShares` creates a permanent gap: `totalAssets` grows\nfaster than `HALF_SLOPE × totalShares²`. When `previewWithdraw` uses `divUp` (correct per spec) and then subtracts, the\noperand order produces an underflow. With `OFFSET = 0`, no offset term closes this gap.\n\n**Why the deployer has no warning:**\n\n- `initialize(\"MyOffsetCurve\", 2e18, 0)` executes without error.\n- `slope18 = 2e18` passes validation (non-zero, even). `offset18 = 0` is never checked.\n- The contract emits no event, no revert, no log indicating the broken state.\n- `MAX_SHARES` is computed as `sub(sqrt(uMAX/uUNIT), wrap(0))` — the full unreduced range, which appears normal.\n- The first deposit succeeds. Only on the first full-withdrawal preview does the panic surface.\n\n**Impact:**\n\n1. **EIP-4626 spec violation.** `previewWithdraw` MUST NOT revert for valid inputs (`assets ≤ maxWithdraw`). Any\n   integrator, front-end, or aggregator calling `previewWithdraw(totalAssets, ...)` will receive a panic revert.\n2. **Full-pool withdrawal query permanently broken.** A depositor cannot preview their own full exit amount from a\n   zero-offset curve instance.\n3. **Non-upgradeable — redeployment required.** The broken `OFFSET` is immutable after initialization. Any vaults that\n   have registered this curve address must be repointed, which may not be possible depending on vault upgrade patterns.\n4. **Silent misconfiguration.** The deployer receives no feedback that `offset18 = 0` is semantically invalid. The\n   inconsistency between validated `slope18` and unvalidated `offset18` creates a false sense of security: if one\n   parameter is checked, a deployer reasonably assumes all are.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n**Option A — Reject `offset18 = 0` in `initialize()` (Recommended):** Mirror the existing `slope18` validation pattern\nand add a matching guard for `offset18`:\n\n```solidity\n// OffsetProgressiveCurve.sol — initialize(), ~L62\nif (slope18 == 0 || slope18 % 2 != 0) revert OffsetProgressiveCurve_InvalidSlope();\nif (offset18 == 0) revert OffsetProgressiveCurve_InvalidOffset();   // <-- ADD THIS\n\nSLOPE      = wrap(slope18);\nHALF_SLOPE = wrap(slope18 / 2);\nOFFSET     = wrap(offset18);\n```\n\nAdd a corresponding custom error:\n\n```solidity\nerror OffsetProgressiveCurve_InvalidOffset();\n```\n\nThis is a one-line fix that closes the misconfiguration window entirely and makes the validation symmetric with\n`slope18`.",
      "proofOfConcept": "// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\n// initialize() Missing offset18 Validation — OFFSET=0 Inherits F-022 previewWithdraw Underflow\n//\n// Root cause: initialize() validates slope18 (non-zero, even) but places NO constraint\n// on offset18. When offset18=0, OFFSET = wrap(0), and OffsetProgressiveCurve becomes\n// MATHEMATICALLY IDENTICAL to ProgressiveCurve with the same slope.\n//  (previewWithdraw underflow on full withdrawal) directly applies.\n//\n// Math proof (slope=2e18, HALF_SLOPE=1e18, OFFSET=0):\n//   deposit 2 wei: inner = square(wrap(0)) + div(wrap(2), 1e18) = 0 + 2 = 2\n//                  sharesUD = sqrt(2*1e18) - 0 = floor(1414213562.37...) = 1414213562 raw\n//   previewWithdraw(2, 2, 1414213562):\n//     s = 1414213562 + 0 = 1414213562\n//     deduct = divUp(2, 1e18) = 2\n//     square(s) = floor(1414213562^2 / 1e18) = 1 (since 1414213562^2 = 1999999... < 2e18)\n//     inner = sub(1, 2) → UNDERFLOW → REVERT\n//\n// Confirmed by Diligence audit: \"An OffsetProgressiveCurve with offset zero behaves\n// exactly like the ProgressiveCurve with the same slope.\"\n// \n//\n// RUN: forge test --match-test \"test_F028\" -vvv\n\nimport { Test } from \"forge-std/src/Test.sol\";\nimport { console2 } from \"forge-std/src/console2.sol\";\nimport { TransparentUpgradeableProxy } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/transparent/TransparentUpgradeableProxy.sol\";\nimport { OffsetProgressiveCurve } from \"src/protocol/curves/OffsetProgressiveCurve.sol\";\nimport { ProgressiveCurve } from \"src/protocol/curves/ProgressiveCurve.sol\";\n\ncontract OffsetProgressiveCurveF028Test is Test {\n    OffsetProgressiveCurve curve;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        OffsetProgressiveCurve impl = new OffsetProgressiveCurve();\n        TransparentUpgradeableProxy proxy = new TransparentUpgradeableProxy(address(impl), address(this), \"\");\n        curve = OffsetProgressiveCurve(address(proxy));\n        // Initialise with offset18 = 0 — should revert or be guarded, but is NOT\n        curve.initialize(\"TestOPC-F028\", 2e18, 0);\n    }\n\n    // Demonstrates that OFFSET=0 is accepted without error\n    function test_F028_ZeroOffsetAccepted() public {\n        // initialize() did not revert → offset18=0 is silently permitted\n        uint256 maxShares = curve.MAX_SHARES();\n        console2.log(\"MAX_SHARES:\", maxShares);\n        // Succeeds — demonstrates missing validation\n    }\n\n    // Demonstrates that previewWithdraw reverts exactly as in F-022\n    function test_F028_previewWithdrawUnderflowsIdenticalToF022() public {\n        uint256 depositAssets = 2;\n\n        // Step 1: compute shares for a tiny deposit (empty pool)\n        uint256 sharesOut = curve.previewDeposit(depositAssets, 0, 0);\n        console2.log(\"previewDeposit(2 wei, empty pool) = shares:\", sharesOut);\n        // Expected: floor(sqrt(2*1e18)) = 1414213562 (same as ProgressiveCurve with slope=2e18)\n\n        // Step 2: previewRedeem returns fewer assets (rounding loss — dust trapped)\n        uint256 redeemReturn = curve.previewRedeem(sharesOut, sharesOut, depositAssets);\n        console2.log(\"previewRedeem(all shares)   = assets:\", redeemReturn);\n        assertLt(redeemReturn, depositAssets, \"Untrapped dust: redeem should return < deposited\");\n\n        // Step 3: previewWithdraw(2, 2, 1414213562) REVERTS with arithmetic underflow\n        // divUp(2, 1e18) = 2 raw > square(1414213562) = 1 raw → sub() underflows\n        console2.log(\"Calling previewWithdraw(2, 2, sharesOut) - expect REVERT:\");\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        curve.previewWithdraw(depositAssets, depositAssets, sharesOut);\n        console2.log(\"PASS: previewWithdraw reverted as expected (F-022 inherited)\");\n    }\n\n    // Demonstrates that the fix would be to require offset18 > 0 in initialize()\n    function test_F028_FixDemonstration_NonZeroOffsetPreventsUnderflow() public {\n        // Deploy a fresh OPC with offset18 = 1e18 (i.e., OFFSET = 1.0)\n        OffsetProgressiveCurve impl2 = new OffsetProgressiveCurve();\n        TransparentUpgradeableProxy proxy2 = new TransparentUpgradeableProxy(address(impl2), address(this), \"\");\n        OffsetProgressiveCurve curveSafe = OffsetProgressiveCurve(address(proxy2));\n        curveSafe.initialize(\"TestOPC-Fixed\", 2e18, 1e18); // offset = 1.0\n\n        uint256 sharesOut = curveSafe.previewDeposit(2, 0, 0);\n        console2.log(\"[Fixed OPC OFFSET=1.0] previewDeposit(2 wei) =\", sharesOut);\n        // With non-zero OFFSET, tiny deposits may yield 0 shares but previewWithdraw\n        // does NOT underflow (F-029 is separate — full-pool off-by-1, not underflow)\n    }\n}",
